sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-goals-17> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Because headless planaria mounted a regenerative response with no triggering injury, the authors argue this is consistent with the idea that a missing-tissue response may not be necessary for regeneration and that subtle internal dynamics may suffice to initiate change long after a process seems to have stabilized.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Regeneration can start without injury, so a missing-tissue response may be unnecessary";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Pio-Lopez L, Bischof J, LaPalme JV, Levin M, “The scaling of goals from cellular to anatomical homeostasis: an evolutionary simulation, experiment and analysis”, Interface focus (2023), doi:10.1098/rsfs.2022.0072; section “Discussion”. Scope: Planarian regeneration (Dugesia japonica)"
}
